# Freeze line endings byte-for-byte.
#
# Every tracked text file here is LF today (`git ls-files --eol` reports 184 lf,
# 13 binary, 2 empty) and `core.autocrlf` is unset. That combination is fragile:
# a checkout on Windows, or an editor saving through a WSL mount, can silently
# renormalise a whole file. The change then arrives as a whole-file diff that
# buries the one line actually being edited.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in both directions, so git stores and
# checks out exactly the bytes it was given. It does not rewrite anything that
# is already committed.
* -text
